        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Kebra Nagast</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1314 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Made by</span><span class="info-stat-val">Attributed to Nebure Id Yeshaq of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksumite-empire">Aksum</a>; its colophon names a team of Ethiopian clerics who translated it into Geʽez from Arabic, in a tradition that gives Coptic as the first language</span></div>
